    "perplexity": {
      "description": "White of the Eye is the soundtrack to the 1987 British thriller of the same name, credited to Nick Mason and Rick Fenn and originally issued on Parlophone. Blending jazz, rock, and progressive textures, it leans on atmospheric instrumentals rather than conventional songs, with Mason’s percussion and Fenn’s guitar work creating a tense, cinematic mood that fits the film’s unsettling tone.\n\nThe album is notable as one of Mason’s more elusive solo-era projects, and it reflects his willingness to move beyond Pink Floyd’s arena-scale psychodrama into compact, mood-driven composition. Originally tied to the film’s release, it later gained renewed attention through remastered editions and inclusion in the Unattended Luggage box set, which helped restore the soundtrack’s place in Mason’s catalog.",
